WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:19.471
This is the Daily Karma. Today’s practice is zanshin: after the arrow. Find a supported position. Let your eyes close, or rest gently on the painting.

2
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:40.452
Feel where your body meets the chair or floor. Soften your hands. Give gravity permission to carry a little more of your weight.

3
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:07.520
Place attention where breathing feels clearest: the nose, chest, or belly. Receive each breath without needing to hold on to it.

4
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:36.446
Zanshin is remaining mind: the attention that stays after the act is finished. In archery the posture is held after the arrow has gone. The shot is not over at release.

5
00:01:51.000 --> 00:02:03.399
The archer, bow still open, eyes still down the range, long after the arrow has landed. Nothing is being achieved. The form is simply being completed.

6
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:29.985
Notice what your body is doing with these words. Soften around the eyes, the hands, and the belly. Keep only the effort needed to stay present.

7
00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:57.102
Finish this breath all the way out before taking the next. Let the ending be as attended as the beginning. Most of us leave early.

8
00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:26.588
For a little while, I will be quiet. Let thoughts pass like weather over a wide landscape. When attention wanders, return with patience.

9
00:03:55.000 --> 00:04:04.474
Still here. Still breathing. Nothing special needs to happen. This quiet awareness is already a useful way of meeting your life.

10
00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:27.124
Finish one thing properly today. Close the conversation rather than drifting out of it. Put the tool back. Stay for the last minute of something.

11
00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:52.288
Take one fuller breath. Feel the space beyond your body and let your eyes open in their own time. Thank you for practicing with Karma.
